20,2,,status,Toshio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
21,2,,status,Rin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
22,2,,status,Shion,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
23,2,,status,Mizuki,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
24,2,,status,Yumi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
25,2,1,talk,Rin,,"Setting up every morning takes way too long, and those unplanned shuffles are a total nightmare. We can't have a chaotic system.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
26,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"We are paying for empty space, and every single move costs us thousands of yen. Constant changes are financially irresponsible.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
27,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"Some people arrive much later than others, and the current plan leaves too many people without windows. It's not equitable.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
28,2,1,talk,Shion,,"The noise levels vary wildly across the room, and it takes days to get a chair and monitor set up correctly.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
29,2,1,talk,Yumi,,Sitting together actually helps us work faster and helps new people learn the ropes just by listening.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
30,2,2,talk,Rin,,"If it takes nine minutes just to plug in, a free-for-all sounds exhausting.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"Exactly. If we move people around frequently, the facilities quotes will drain our budget.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"If we go with a first-come, first-served system, the early birds always get the best spots. That's not fair.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,2,talk,Shion,,"And if we move constantly, I'll never get my workstation adjusted to a comfortable setting.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"But if we stay in fixed blocks, we might miss out on those spontaneous helpful conversations.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,3,talk,Rin,,"Maybe rotating? But that sounds like more of those ""fortnight of interruptions"" shuffles.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,3,talk,Toshio,,Rotating blocks would be a recurring expense for power and network. It's inefficient.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"Fixed desks seem the most stable, but we have to decide who gets the window seats.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,3,talk,Shion,,Fixed desks are the only way to ensure I'm not stuck in a high-decibel zone with a bad chair.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,3,talk,Yumi,,"I agree that fixed desks help, as long as we group people who actually need to talk.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,4,talk,Rin,,I just don't want to waste my gaps between meetings. Fixed seems safest.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,4,talk,Toshio,,I concur. Fixed desks minimize costs and administrative waste.,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,4,talk,Mizuki,,"As long as we assign them logically and not just by habit, I'm for it.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,4,talk,Shion,,It's the only logical choice for physical and mental comfort.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,4,talk,Yumi,,"If we group by function, we keep the synergy. I'm in.","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,3,,status,Toshio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
